#
#            176dadc — the exhibits are computed at render time from the latest
#              calculation, which is what makes them agree with the summary
#              page and equally what means a recalculation moves every figure a
#              re-render would produce. `POST /report/render` overwrote the
#              stored PDF for the current version with no state guard, so a
#              published engagement whose client holds v3 — in board minutes, in
#              an auditor's file — could be re-rendered into a different
#              document under the same version number with a different concluded
#              value, and nobody outside this system could tell. A delivered
#              version's bytes are now written once; a new version is how
#              revised figures are published, which leaves both documents in the
#              history.
